{"entryId":"1657","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1657:1","sourceSha256":"2ad9cddd2ae1eb04a41020cc914b915ae88f283364fc7e7a6aae85545edc5169","englishSha256":"8483a13fb1398b67b8a31ca4655bff44eadc8e57627e6620d1dbaeb56f9e8143","citations":[{"id":"1657:1:citation-01","he":[12,59],"en":[309,324],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_164b.14"},"reference":"Bava Batra 164b:14","assessment":"The Bavli distinguishes the tied document from the separate praise of the orderly writing in Psalms. This is the second event. It retains Shimon’s denial that he wrote it.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 164b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_164b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 164b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_164b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1657:1:citation-02","he":[187,214],"en":[421,450],"target":{"entry":920,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 920:1","assessment":"The reciprocal Heilprin entry explicitly discusses the same maxim and Semag interpretation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 920:1","target":{"entry":920,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"1657:1:citation-03","he":[222,258],"en":[452,481],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_Mitzvot_Gadol%2C_Negative_Commandments_9.1"},"reference":"Sefer Mitzvot Gadol, Negative Commandments 9:1","assessment":"The checked Semag explicitly distinguishes speaking before enemies from speaking before friends. This confirms the interpretation Heilprin proceeds to question.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Mitzvot Gadol, Negative Commandments 9:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_Mitzvot_Gadol%2C_Negative_Commandments_9.1"},"witness":"Munkatch, 1901"}]},{"id":"1657:1:citation-04","he":[469,499],"en":[848,861],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashbam_on_Bava_Batra_164b.15.2"},"reference":"Rashbam on Bava Batra 164b:15:2","assessment":"Rashbam and Rashi explain differently how praise may lead to disparagement. The claim that praise before friends is included remains Heilprin’s inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashbam on Bava Batra 164b:15:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashbam_on_Bava_Batra_164b.15.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashbam on Bava Batra 164b:15:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashbam_on_Bava_Batra_164b.15.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashi on Arakhin 16a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Arakhin_16a.3.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1657:1:citation-05","he":[469,499],"en":[866,883],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Arakhin_16a.3.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Arakhin 16a:3:1","assessment":"Rashbam and Rashi explain differently how praise may lead to disparagement. The claim that praise before friends is included remains Heilprin’s inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Arakhin 16a:3:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Arakhin_16a.3.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashbam on Bava Batra 164b:15:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashbam_on_Bava_Batra_164b.15.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashbam on Bava Batra 164b:15:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashbam_on_Bava_Batra_164b.15.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Keep Semag’s allowance before friends and Heilprin’s objection distinct from the source interpretations of Rashbam and Rashi.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 164b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_164b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 164b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_164b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{